# Vet Lab Results API: demo walkthrough
#
# 1. Start the API:  npm run dev
# 2. Click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.
#
# Requests later in the file reuse the patient IDs from steps 1 and 1b automatically.
# All data here is made up.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 0. Health check: is the API up?
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1. Register a patient (Biscuit, a dog)
# @name createPatient
POST {{baseUrl}}/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Biscuit",
  "species": "Dog"
}

### 1b. Register a second patient (Mochi, a cat)
# @name createPatient2
POST {{baseUrl}}/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mochi",
  "species": "Cat"
}

###
@patientId = {{createPatient.response.body.$.patient.id}}
@patientId2 = {{createPatient2.response.body.$.patient.id}}

### 2. Biscuit: glucose within range → NORMAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "testCode": "GLU",
  "value": 98,
  "unit": "mg/dL",
  "referenceLow": 74,
  "referenceHigh": 143,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-01T09:15:00.000Z"
}

### 3. Biscuit: liver enzyme above range → HIGH
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "testCode": "ALT",
  "value": 212,
  "unit": "U/L",
  "referenceLow": 10,
  "referenceHigh": 125,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-03T14:30:00.000Z"
}

### 4. Biscuit: potassium below range, a decimal value → LOW
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "testCode": "K",
  "value": 3.1,
  "unit": "mmol/L",
  "referenceLow": 3.5,
  "referenceHigh": 5.8,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-05T08:45:00.000Z"
}

### 5. Biscuit: no reference range from the lab → UNKNOWN (never assumed NORMAL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "testCode": "SDMA",
  "value": 16,
  "unit": "ug/dL",
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-07T11:00:00.000Z"
}

### 5b. Mochi: kidney value above the feline range → HIGH
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId2}}",
  "testCode": "CREA",
  "value": 2.9,
  "unit": "mg/dL",
  "referenceLow": 0.8,
  "referenceHigh": 2.4,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-06T10:20:00.000Z"
}

### 5c. Mochi: glucose within the feline range → NORMAL
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId2}}",
  "testCode": "GLU",
  "value": 112,
  "unit": "mg/dL",
  "referenceLow": 71,
  "referenceHigh": 159,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-08T16:05:00.000Z"
}

### 6. Biscuit's full history, newest first (none of Mochi's results)
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}/results

### 6b. Mochi's history: only her two results
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId2}}/results

### 7. Biscuit: only results that need attention (LOW, HIGH, UNKNOWN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}/results?abnormal=true

### 7b. Mochi: only results that need attention
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId2}}/results?abnormal=true

### 8a. Bad input → 400 listing each problem (wrong type, plus a server-set field the client may not send)
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "testCode": "GLU",
  "value": "high",
  "unit": "mg/dL",
  "referenceLow": 74,
  "referenceHigh": 143,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-08T09:00:00.000Z",
  "flag": "NORMAL"
}

### 8b. Reversed reference range → 400 pointing at referenceLow
POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-results
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
  "testCode": "GLU",
  "value": 98,
  "unit": "mg/dL",
  "referenceLow": 143,
  "referenceHigh": 74,
  "collectedAt": "2026-10-08T09:00:00.000Z"
}

### 9. Typo in the query parameter → 400, not a silently unfiltered list
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/{{patientId}}/results?abnormal=ture

### 10. Unknown patient → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/patients/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/results
